// Pull request: #6540 Sigma: PavinLoader fake-driver MSI campaign (MSBuild from %LOCALAPPDATA%, MSBUILDENABLEALLPROPERTYFUNCTIONS, fake dllhost/taskhostw tasks, m
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6540
// Pull request author: fotedev
// Change: new rule
// Title: Scheduled Task Files Named dllhost or taskhostw Written Outside schtasks.exe
// Sigma ID: d5ba62a1-5139-47f9-992d-a93cdf3f5fb2
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: fotedev
// Date: 2026-10-29 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1053.005
// Description: Detects creation (or modification) of scheduled task files named "dllhost" or "taskhostw" under
//   C:\Windows\System32\Tasks - names masquerading as the legitimate system binaries dllhost.exe /
//   taskhostw.exe. Observed PavinLoader.BAT persistence dropped such task files. In Sysmon
//   file_event (EID 11) the Image field identifies the process that wrote the file; any writer other
//   than schtasks.exe is suspicious. Note that the Task Scheduler service (svchost.exe) writes task
//   XML natively, so extend the filter if your baseline creates these names through other APIs.
// False positives:
//   - Administrative tooling or configuration management that registers tasks with these exact names through APIs other than schtasks.exe
// References:
//   - Verified internal incident report, Trojan.PavinLoader.BAT (Malwarebytes family naming), 2026-10-29
//   - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1053/005/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/a477302bc4d0372ca2d1b32b2981597468776c0c/rules/windows/file_event/file_event_win_schtask_files_dllhost_taskhostw.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\Windows\\System32\\Tasks\\dllhost" or FolderPath endswith "\\Windows\\System32\\Tasks\\taskhostw") and (not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\schtasks.exe"))
